course: dictionary
lesson: 4555
title: Heavily: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Heavily» can mean three things: with great weight, a lot, or slowly and tired. Context clues tell you which meaning fits. Look at the words next to it, such as rain, sigh or guarded.
explain: Try the swap test. «She sat down heavily after a long day» means she sat down slowly and wearily, as if tired. Put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
explain: «Some borders are marked by walls and fences, such as the heavily guarded border between North and South Korea.» Here heavily means very strongly. The border is not heavy. It is watched very closely, so guarded and heavily work together.
fact: Heavily means in a heavy way, with great weight or force.
fact: Heavily also means very much or to a great degree, as in «it rained heavily».
fact: Heavily can mean slowly and with effort, as if you are tired or sad, as in «she sighed heavily».
fact: «Taxed his people heavily» means taxed them a lot.
fact: Words like rain, snow, breathe and depends often show you which meaning of heavily is used.
exercise: «She sighed heavily when the test was over.» What does heavily mean here? | With great weight | Very loudly and clearly | *Slowly, as if tired or sad | Quickly and happily
exercise: «It was raining heavily when we left school.» What does heavily mean here? | Quietly | With great weight | Slowly | *A lot
exercise: Which sentence uses heavily to mean with great weight? | «He sighed heavily after the match.» | *«The heavily loaded cart creaked up the hill.» | «The town is heavily guarded by the police.» | «It snowed heavily all night.»
test: «Solomon taxed his people heavily.» What does heavily mean? | *A lot | Quietly | Lightly | Gently and kindly
test: What does «breathed heavily» suggest about a character? | *Tired, scared or worn out | Very quiet and calm | Happy and excited | Cold and wet
exam: In «The town depends heavily on tourists», what does heavily mean? | Lightly | Carefully | Very little | *A lot
